<title>JAPAN: Credit Saison falls on recent rating cut.</title>
<headline>Credit Saison falls on recent rating cut.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Saison Co Ltd fell on Friday morning due to the lingering effect of a recent rating downgrade, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0052 GMT, the shares were down 70 yen at 2,530, the 10th most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse with trade at 2.072 million shares.  </p>
<p>On Thursday, Goldman Sachs cut Credit Saison's rating from an &quot;outperformer&quot; to an &quot;average performer&quot;.</p>
